# api-deejaytools — names this service reads. Names only: the values live
# in Doppler (mini-app-polis-ecosystem / dev locally, prd on Railway). Run
# under `doppler run -- …`; do not copy this to .env — nothing reads it.
#
# Uncommented names are required in Doppler's dev config, and
# `uv run check-doppler-keys` checks dev holds every one. Commented names
# are optional: the code has a default, only production reads them, or the
# value comes from elsewhere. What the Discord channels post, and what is
# not carried over from deejaytools-api: docs/OPERATIONS.md.
#
# Prefixed because these live in the shared ecosystem Doppler config next to
# other services' values (including the other Clerk tenant's CLERK_*). They
# are the names deejaytools-api read, so its config carried over unchanged.

# Database. Plain postgresql:// URLs are fine; the app switches to asyncpg.
# Not in Doppler: Railway references its Postgres service, and a local run
# sets it in the shell, which `doppler run` passes through.
# DEEJAYTOOLS_DATABASE_URL=
# OPS-002. Read only by scripts/apply_migrations.py, which runs before the
# app in the start command. Bind it to a role that owns the schema and keep
# DEEJAYTOOLS_DATABASE_URL's role without DDL. Unset locally: the runner
# falls back to DEEJAYTOOLS_DATABASE_URL and logs that the separation is not
# in effect.
# DEEJAYTOOLS_DATABASE_URL_MIGRATIONS=
# Also read only by scripts/apply_migrations.py: BOOTSTRAP_MIGRATIONS=true
# marks every migration except those named in BOOTSTRAP_EXCLUDE as applied
# without running them, for adopting an existing database. Without
# BOOTSTRAP_EXCLUDE it refuses. Unset otherwise.
# BOOTSTRAP_MIGRATIONS=
# BOOTSTRAP_EXCLUDE=

# Auth — the one trusted Clerk instance for this environment. Unset means
# every authenticated request is rejected. Also read by
# scripts/backfill_principals.py, which makes existing users principals of
# this issuer.
DEEJAYTOOLS_CLERK_ISSUER=
DEEJAYTOOLS_CLERK_JWKS_URL=

# CORS — comma-separated origins.
DEEJAYTOOLS_CORS_ORIGINS=

# Doppler sets it per config (development in dev, production in prd). It
# wins over RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_NAME, so the two must agree; unset resolves
# from that, else local.
# ENVIRONMENT=

# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' logger. Default INFO.
# LOGGING_LEVEL=

# Set by Railway on every deploy: the commit GET /version reports. Unset
# locally.
# RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=

# Sentry — the shared apis project (also read by api-kaianolevine-com);
# events are told apart by the `service` tag. Unset turns it off.
# SENTRY_DSN_APIS=

# CD-036. Request metrics to CloudWatch, published in production only, with
# the same API identity as api-kaianolevine-com (shared config). Unset keys
# fall back to boto3's default credential chain. AWS_REGION defaults to
# us-east-1.
# AWS_REGION=
EVALUATION_QUEUE_PRODUCER_KEY_ID=
EVALUATION_QUEUE_PRODUCER_SECRET=

# Feedback email (POST /v1/feedback) through Brevo. Unset: feedback is
# accepted and no email is sent. The fleet's one Brevo key.
BREVO_API_KEY=

# Discord notifications (docs/OPERATIONS.md, "Discord notifications"). The
# fleet's shared channels, so unprefixed. Each channel reads its own webhook
# and falls back to DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL; with neither set, that channel is
# off (logged once) and nothing is sent.
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL_ERRORS=
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL_ACTIVITY=
# false mutes the per-request "data changed" feed; faults and "song added"
# still post. Default true.
# NOTIFY_DATA_CHANGES=
# Which events each environment posts, as JSON: environment name to event
# names (data_changed, fault). An environment with no entry posts every
# event. Defaults in config.py; development leaves out data_changed.
# DISCORD_NOTIFY_EVENTS={"production": ["data_changed", "fault"], "development": ["fault"]}

# Google Drive (deejaytools-api DRIVE.md). Both are required by every Drive
# call; with either missing, uploads and drive_jobs fail with "Google Drive
# environment variables are not configured". GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON is the
# fleet's one service account's JSON key file, the same value the cogs read.
# Scope used: drive.file only.
GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_PARENT_FOLDER_ID=

# Scheduler (session status advance, queue auto-fill, drive_jobs). Runs once
# at startup, then every TICK_INTERVAL_MS (default 30000). DISABLE_SCHEDULER=1
# turns it off
# (only the string "1"). It is also off whenever ENVIRONMENT=test. Locally, set DISABLE_SCHEDULER=1 on the command
# line (see README): it is not in Doppler, so `doppler run` passes it through.
# TICK_INTERVAL_MS=
# DISABLE_SCHEDULER=
# GET /internal/tick requires x-tick-secret to equal this. Unset: the route
# refuses every call (fails closed). An empty value is a set secret, so leave
# the line commented out rather than blank when there is no secret.
# TICK_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tests only
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# external tooling: read by tests/integration/conftest.py, never by the app.
# The integration tests' database (default a local deejaytools_test).
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# The conformance suite (conformance/, docs/CONFORMANCE.md). Its database is
# DEEJAYTOOLS_DATABASE_URL, or DATABASE_URL when that is unset; required for
# the suite. INTEGRATION_BASE_URL points it at a running server instead of
# the in-process app (an origin, no path), INTEGRATION_JWKS_PORT fixes the
# stand-in Clerk JWKS server's port for such a target, INTEGRATION_EXTRA_
# MIGRATIONS names a folder of the target's migrations after its baseline,
# and INTEGRATION_TICK_SECRET is sent as x-tick-secret.
# DATABASE_URL=
# INTEGRATION_BASE_URL=
# INTEGRATION_JWKS_PORT=
# INTEGRATION_EXTRA_MIGRATIONS=
# INTEGRATION_TICK_SECRET=
